<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Domnall Mór Ua Briain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1194</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Domnall Mor O'Brien, Donal Mór O'Brien</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Domnall Mór <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obrien-dynasty">Ua Briain</a> was king of Thomond and, at times, of Munster from 1168. He submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> in 1171 but fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Normans</a> for much of his reign, defeating them at Thurles in 1174. A generous church patron, he founded or endowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-cross-abbey">Holy Cross Abbey</a> and St Mary's Cathedral in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/limerick">Limerick</a>.</p></div>
